# Portfolio Coding Standards

## Stack

- **Frontend**: React 19 + Vite, deployed to GitHub Pages at `/Portfolio_Website/`
- **Backend**: ASP.NET Core 8 Web API, SQLite (dev) / PostgreSQL (prod)

## Conventions

- Content lives in `frontend/src/data/resumeContent.js` — edit copy there, not inline in components
- API calls go through `frontend/src/services/api.js`; use `VITE_API_BASE_URL` for the backend URL
- Use existing CSS variables in `index.css`; avoid inline styles unless required (e.g. Three.js canvas)
- Admin routes (`/admin`, `/admin/dashboard`) are private — never link from public navbar

## React

- Functional components with hooks only
- Lazy-load heavy deps (Three.js) and disable on mobile / `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Analytics failures must not break UX — catch silently in `useAnalytics`

## Backend

- Enrich visitor metadata via `IVisitorMetadataService`, not in controllers
- Use `GeoLocationService.NormalizeLocationLabel()` for dashboard location display
- Private/localhost IPs return `"Local Development"`, not `"Local"`
- JWT required on `/api/analytics/dashboard`; rate-limit contact submissions

## Do not edit

- `.cursor/plans/` plan files
